<section class="work-panel v4-review" id="code-checks"><div class="panel-title"><h2>Selected member · source vs code</h2><span>Spacing checks are not a structural design</span></div><div class="v3-section-body"><div id="code-member-summary"></div><div id="code-results"></div><details id="station-register"><summary>Exact trial station offsets</summary><div id="station-table"></div><button id="export-stations">Export trial stations · CSV</button></details><details id="trial-controls"><summary>Preview a calculated detailing scenario</summary><p>No project cover has been confirmed. The trial button uses <strong>40 mm for a column, 25 mm for a beam, or 50 mm for a rectangular footing</strong> as explicitly assumed calculation inputs, not as an adopted Basanti detail. Edit or clear them. No new longitudinal steel is designed. The footing input enables rectangular mesh arithmetic; it does not design the foundation.</p><form id="trial-form"><div class="v3-control-grid"><label>Layout basis<select id="trial-mode"><option value="source">Source only · unpositioned links withheld</option><option value="trial">Conditional calculated trial</option></select></label><label>Trial nominal cover to outside link · mm<input id="trial-cover" type="number" min="1" max="250" step="1" placeholder="Unconfirmed"></label><label>Clear column height H · mm<input id="trial-height" type="number" min="1" max="15000" step="1" placeholder="Model face height, if available"></label><label>Effective beam depth d · mm<input id="trial-depth" type="number" min="1" max="2000" step="1" placeholder="Calculated from cover and bottom layer"></label><label>Trial close-link maximum pitch · mm<input id="trial-end-spacing" type="number" min="1" max="500" step="1" placeholder="Derived from the limit"></label><label>Trial middle maximum pitch · mm<input id="trial-mid-spacing" type="number" min="1" max="500" step="1" placeholder="Source pitch, capped for this check"></label><label>First / last link from each clear face · mm<input id="trial-first" type="number" min="0" max="50" step="1" value="50"></label></div><div class="view-controls"><button type="button" id="preview-trial">Preview labelled trial</button><button type="submit">Apply entered scenario</button><button type="button" id="restore-source">Return to source-only view</button></div><p id="trial-status" role="status"></p></form></details><p>Trial loops show spacing planes with schematic corners. Hook bends, joint/footing confinement and full-height confinement triggers need coordinated detailing. The same trial station coordinates drive the drawing, 3D and table.</p></div></section>
<section class="work-panel v4-review" id="bbs-study"><div class="panel-title"><h2>Bar bending schedule · calculation study</h2><button id="export-bbs">Export BBS study · CSV</button></div><div class="v3-section-body"><p><strong>Shown geometry is not an issued cutting length.</strong> Counts below describe displayed paths or trial station planes. Steel mass uses stated density 7,850 kg/m³; a sharp-corner display loop is not a bend-corrected fabrication shape.</p><div id="bbs-summary"></div><div id="bbs-grouped"></div><div id="lap-area-check"></div><details id="development-controls"><summary>Development, lap-area and cutting arithmetic</summary><div class="v3-control-grid"><label>Entered / confirmed steel grade<select id="steel-grade"><option value="">Not supplied</option><option>Fe250</option><option>Fe415</option><option>Fe500</option></select></label><label>Entered / confirmed concrete grade<select id="concrete-grade"><option value="">Not supplied</option><option>M20</option><option>M25</option><option>M30</option><option>M35</option><option>M40+</option></select></label></div><div id="development-result"></div><p>Table 4.3 applies to fully stressed straight deformed bars in tension. Grades do not establish anchorage shape, demand, lap location or approval. The source footing 60φ note is not used as a universal lap rule.</p><h3>Explicit cutting-length arithmetic</h3><p id="cut-bar-label"></p><form id="cut-form"><div class="v3-control-grid"><label>Tangent straight total to check · mm<input id="cut-straight" type="number" min="0" step=".1" placeholder="Shown straight preview, if suitable"></label><label>Additional start straight / lap · mm<input id="cut-start" type="number" min="0" step="1" placeholder="Unknown; not zero"></label><label>Additional end straight / lap · mm<input id="cut-end" type="number" min="0" step="1" placeholder="Unknown; not zero"></label><label>Shape bends<select id="cut-bend-mode"><option value="unknown">Not established</option><option value="none">Explicitly no bends</option><option value="entered">Entered identical centreline arcs</option></select></label><label>Centreline bend radius · mm<input id="cut-radius" type="number" min="1" step="1" placeholder="Not a bend-test mandrel"></label><label>Angle of each entered arc · degrees<input id="cut-angle" type="number" min="1" max="360" step="1"></label><label>Number of identical arcs<input id="cut-arc-count" type="number" min="1" max="20" step="1"></label></div><button type="submit">Check entered cut arithmetic</button><p id="cut-result" role="status"></p></form><p>Formula: tangent straights + specified additional straights + Σ(radius × angle × π/180). Do not add a generic bend allowance to a centreline arc again. Bend radii and shape remain unconfirmed; no final fabrication release is generated.</p></details></div></section>
